meta {
  name: Get EMA
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/ema/TSLA261016C00360000?timespan=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: M5
  ~count: 200
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # EMA on an Option Contract

  Computes the configured EMA periods (app.engine.ema-periods, default
  8/20/50/100/200/600) over an option contract's closes, reusing the SAME
  EmaCalculator the stock endpoint uses. Inspection only.

  ## Path
  - `{occSymbol}` — OCC option code, e.g. TSLA261016C00360000.

  ## Query
  - `timespan` — bar granularity (default M5). Native only (M1/M5/.../Y).
  - `count`    — bars to fetch (default = app.options.bar-count; option max 1200).

  ## Response (200)
  { optionSymbol, timespan, barsUsed, lastClose,
    emaValues: { "8": ..., "20": ..., ... },   // "INSUFFICIENT_DATA" if too few bars
    periods: [ ... ] }

  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid timespan.
  - `502` — Webull market-data error (e.g. 403 if US_OPTION not subscribed).
  - `503` — no bars for the contract.
}
